<p>Iran’s supreme leader, Ayatollah Mojtaba Khamenei, said Thursday that Tehran would protect its “nuclear and missile capabilities” as national assets, in a statement read by a state television anchor for National Persian Gulf Day. The statement came as President Trump seeks to curb those programs through airstrikes and a wider deal to reinforce a three-week ceasefire in the war involving Iran, the United States and Israel. Khamenei also said Iran would create “new legal frameworks” or a new management system for the Strait of Hormuz and would eliminate what he called hostile enemy abuses of the waterway. Reports citing Reuters said the channel has been closed two months into the conflict, disrupting about 20% of global oil and gas flows, while a U.S. Navy blockade has been stopping Iranian oil tankers from reaching the sea.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/pDdSxsSha2E9A_iTZ3sq5nmQlpfjb2krrePMGQ9QmavFBpbB1YF136sFGHk2juZFQZ5c0d_OGE-nO6Xq4lSeK59wgr3YkKB3Ql3KuvsgYvhajG9g03jvraBnepO_tzYwblPSFaW3EZYkOc9dLUBTupFBJt6Ha9zv1jgfNN0vztHb0BNQf44W2biKiLRdoT8fKoJ-mKl4nXmki7cHIUyFfmd-21_RsNWlcCOaRVYUd8AqSQ3lrzQsp_08HWmlr5sl1fDffJiiiUmWdUvIaw' alt='A tanker unloads crude oil at a terminal after transiting the Strait of Hormuz.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Iranian economy: Khamenei’s remarks came as reports described Iran’s economy as reeling, adding domestic pressure to the diplomatic standoff.</li><li>Gulf appeal: Khamenei said the new management of Hormuz would bring calm, progress and economic benefits to all Gulf nations.</li><li>Leadership visibility: Khamenei has not appeared publicly since he took over after his father was killed in the war’s opening airstrikes.</li></ul><blockquote>Today, two months after the largest military deployment and aggression by the world’s bullies in the region, and the United States’ disgraceful defeat in its plans, a new chapter is unfolding for the Persian Gulf and the strait of Hormuz - Ayatollah Mojtaba Khamenei</blockquote><h3